	"description": "Interactive Susuwatari (soot sprites) wallpaper inspired by Studio Ghibli films. These cute dust bunnies run away from your mouse cursor with realistic physics and leave soot trails behind. Features customizable size, count, flee distance, acceleration, and audio-reactive spikes that pulse and rotate to the beat of your music. Each Susuwatari has a unique rotation and orientation, creating diverse visual patterns when music plays. They also pulse in size to bass frequencies, creating a rhythmic breathing effect. SMART SLEEP SYSTEM: Configure specific hours (e.g., 22:00 to 06:00) and volume threshold (0-100%) - Susuwatari sleep during configured hours only when audio is BELOW the threshold. Set 10% to sleep during quiet moments, 50% to stay awake during most music, or 0% to ignore volume completely. Perfect customization for any audio environment! Move your mouse rapidly in circles around a Susuwatari to make it dizzy - it will show 'X' eyes and wobble around until it recovers! Make zigzag movements away from the Susuwatari to trigger a scatter effect that spreads all sprites randomly across the canvas! Features automatic collection system - Susuwatari automatically collect coal stones and colored stars when they touch them. Large coal explodes the sprite into dust! Shoes act as physical obstacles. Includes particle effects like smoke explosions and soot stains when they disappear.",
